<title>FINLAND: Finnish August EU-harmonised CPI rises 1.1 pct yr/.</title>
<headline>Finnish August EU-harmonised CPI rises 1.1 pct yr/.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Finnish consumer price index partially harmonised to European Union standards rose 1.1 percent year-on-year in August after a 1.1 percent rise in July, Statistics Finland (SF) said on Monday in a statement.</p>
<p>				August 1996     July 1996   August 1995</p>
<p> Yr/Yr			 +1.1 pct	  +1.1 pct     +0.4 pct</p>
<p> Mth/Mth			N/A pct	  -0.2 pct     -0.1 pct</p>
<p> Index (base 1994=100)    102.1	     102.3	  101.01</p>
<p>According to SF's regular national method of calculation, Finnish consumer prices fell 0.2 percent in August on July and rose 0.4 percent year-on-year, it said.  </p>
<p>			    August 1996	 July 1996    August 1995</p>
<p> Yr/yr		     +0.4 pct	    +0.5 pct	+0.5 pct</p>
<p> Mth/mth		   -0.2 pct	    -0.1 pct	-0.2 pct</p>
<p> Index (base 1990=100)  112.6		 112.8	   112.1</p>
<p>Six economists' average forecast for the national CPI figure was for a 0.7 percent rise year-on-year and a 0.1 percent rise month-on-month.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki Newsroom +358 - 0 - 680 50 245</p>
